  "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)={x}^{2}(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y(t)) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)={y}^{2}(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x(t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the system of differential equations, select the correct options below.\n\nThe Jacobian determinant of the system at the equilibrium point ${x}^{∗}=[1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ is given as\n\n$$\nJ(1,1)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nAt this point, the system is \n{{field-2}}\nat ${x}^{∗}.$",
